  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Close the Gap: Sufficient, Competent and Motivated Nurses and Midwives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Norwegian Nurses Organisation (NNO/NSF) aims to create democratic, accountable, inclusive and sustainable organisations for nurses and midwives in four countries in Africa; NOMN in Malawi, RNMU in Rwanda, TANNA in Tanzania and ZINA in Zimbawe. Cooperation with NOMN in Malawi (NONM) goes back to 2006, and will be phased out between 2024 and 2026. TANNA/Tanzania and ZINA/Zimbabwe are new partner as of 2024.The aim is to build the organisational and financial capacty of the partners, to be effective watchdog and advocate for nurses and midwives and solution provider for their governments, contributing to a stronger and more resilient health system to deliver Universal Health Coverage (UHC) and good health for all. NNO will evaluate the projects in the four countries. The project includes a focus on nurses and midwives&#x2019; equal opportunity to leadership training and positions (gender equality) and the rights of nurses and midwives with disabilities. It also aims to train nurses and midwives in health-related climate adaptation, in the face of increased climate change and extreme weather related health emergencies. Finally, the project aims to train the nurses and midwives to provide the best possible assistance to patients with disabilities and with SRHR to female patients.</narrative>
  </description>
